It is late in the afternoon, but the rain is not stopping.
I go into the museum café and wait there.
A young man is standing at the till.
"What would you like?" he asks me politely.
"I would like a tea and this Brötchen here," I say.
"The Brötchen with cheese?" the seller asks.
"No, this Brötchen with tomatoes, please," I answer.
He gives me my food and the receipt.
I take my cup and sit down at the large window.
The tea is hot and tastes very good.
I look through the glass at the wet park.
I think about my time in Mexico again.
Half a year ago, my life was completely different.
Back then, I packed my entire life into boxes.
Everything was new and I was often very stressed.
This city was still completely unfamiliar to me.
This tea and this quiet Sunday are doing me really good.
